#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:93
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "For example, ``source [class=\"gd-input\", shape=note, "
#| "fillcolor=\"#fbfaf3\"]`` sets both the light presentation and its dark "
#| "role. Classes do not choose shapes or add labels: write those "
#| "explicitly so the drawing also works in monochrome. Unclassified steps "
#| "use green. This palette is opt-in; do not apply it to artwork whose "
#| "exact colors carry data."
msgid ""
"For example, ``source [class=\"gd-input\", shape=note, "
"fillcolor=\"#fbfaf3\"]`` sets both the light presentation and its dark "
"role. Classes do not choose shapes or add labels. We write those "
"explicitly, so the drawing also works in monochrome. Unclassified steps "
"use green. This palette is opt-in. We do not apply it to artwork whose "
"exact colors carry data."
msgstr ""
"``source [class=\"gd-input\", shape=note, fillcolor=\"#fbfaf3\"]`` legt "
"helle Gestaltung und dunkle Rolle fest. Form und Text entstehen nicht "
"durch die Klasse; geben Sie beides für Schwarzweißdruck ausdrücklich an. "
"Unklassifizierte Schritte sind grün. Wenden Sie die optionale Palette "
"nicht an, wenn exakte Farben Daten ausdrücken."

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:99
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The light DOT attributes remain the PDF master. The book receives an "
#| "SVG without the adaptive stylesheet. Printed HTML selects the light "
#| "scheme too. Keep both palettes legible and test the actual book; "
#| "transparency alone proves neither. The inheritance rule is defined by "
#| "the `CSS color-scheme specification "
#| "<https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-adjust-1/#color-scheme-prop>`_."
msgid ""
"The light DOT attributes remain the PDF master. The book receives an SVG "
"without the adaptive stylesheet. Printed HTML selects the light scheme "
"too. Keep both palettes legible and test the actual book. Transparency "
"alone proves neither. The inheritance rule is defined by the `CSS "
"color-scheme specification "
"<https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-adjust-1/#color-scheme-prop>`_."
msgstr ""
"Die hellen DOT-Attribute bleiben die Druckvorlage. Das Buch erhält SVG "
"ohne anpassbares CSS; HTML-Druck wählt ebenfalls hell. Prüfen Sie beide "
"Paletten und das echte Buch: Transparenz beweist keine Lesbarkeit. Die "
"Vererbung steht in der `CSS-Spezifikation zu color-scheme "
"<https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-adjust-1/#color-scheme-prop>`_."

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:105
msgid "Make the result legible"
msgstr "Das Ergebnis lesbar gestalten"

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:108
msgid ""
"Keep node labels short. Explain a longer rule below the drawing. Prefer "
"one direction for the main path. Label a return edge with its condition. "
"Use shape and text as well as color. A print reader may have no color at "
"all."
msgstr ""
"Halten Sie Knotenbeschriftungen kurz. Längere Regeln gehören unter die "
"Zeichnung. Bevorzugen Sie eine Hauptrichtung und beschriften Sie "
"Rückkanten mit Bedingungen. Nutzen Sie Form und Text neben Farbe; "
"Druckleser haben womöglich keine Farbe."

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:112
msgid ""
"Supply alternative text and a caption. Test narrow browser windows and "
"the PDF page. If a diagram needs tiny type to fit, split it into two "
"drawings. See :doc:`../media` for image and figure sizing."
msgstr ""
"Ergänzen Sie Alternativtext und Bildunterschrift. Prüfen Sie schmale "
"Browserfenster und PDF-Seiten. Braucht das Diagramm winzige Schrift, "
"teilen Sie es. Größen beschreibt :doc:`../media`\\ ."

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:116
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "On narrow screens, captioned diagrams scroll horizontally to keep "
#| "labels readable. Scroll inside the figure; the page itself keeps its "
#| "width."
msgid ""
"On narrow screens, captioned diagrams scroll horizontally to keep labels "
"readable. Scroll inside the figure. The page itself keeps its width."
msgstr ""
"Auf schmalen Bildschirmen scrollen beschriftete Grafiken horizontal in "
"ihrem eigenen Bereich. Die Schrift bleibt lesbar, die Seite behält ihre "
"Breite."

